.TH FREE 1
.SH NAME
free - display physical memory and process capacity
.SH SYNOPSIS
free
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports memory in KiB (1024 physical octets). Ripple C characters contain
16 bits; one 512-cell MMU page occupies one KiB.
.PP
Mem includes the reserved kernel and platform area. User pool reports the
physical memory available to processes. Shared pages count once in used
memory, while process mappings count every reference to a shared page.
The reserved area is unavailable to the user allocator; it is not a measurement
of the kernel's live allocations. Swap is not implemented.
.PP
The process count includes this utility and unreaped zombies. The data/heap
limit includes static program data; it is not an additional malloc allowance.
The legacy profile reports fixed process reservations and has no COW sharing.
.SH OPTIONS
--help displays usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
ps(1), uptime(1)
